WEBVTT

00:02:32.480 --> 00:02:35.130
It's finally Sunday.

00:02:36.160 --> 00:02:39.120
I put on my brand-new white sneakers.

00:02:40.720 --> 00:02:42.860
All right, let's go out!

00:02:58.740 --> 00:03:02.240
If you don't mind TPO, that's what'll happen.

00:03:03.010 --> 00:03:06.000
If you go out in the rain{y season} wearing white sneakers.

00:03:06.000 --> 00:03:07.250
But—!

00:03:11.670 --> 00:03:13.570
A convertible in June!?

00:03:13.570 --> 00:03:15.320
Come on, mind TPO!

00:03:15.610 --> 00:03:18.530
The world is full of things like that! It really irritates me!

00:03:18.530 --> 00:03:22.420
Like carrying golf clubs while getting questioned due to suspicion of being bribed with golfing trips!

00:03:22.420 --> 00:03:24.800
Or getting a red card during stoppage time!

00:03:24.800 --> 00:03:27.170
Or the current Rambo's front line!

00:03:30.300 --> 00:03:32.570
Come on, mind TPO!

00:03:32.800 --> 00:03:33.690
So...

00:03:34.270 --> 00:03:38.180
June brides aren't minding TPO, are they.

00:03:38.470 --> 00:03:39.910
Huh? Why?

00:03:40.270 --> 00:03:42.210
Having a ceremony in the rainy season?

00:03:42.210 --> 00:03:47.690
It's likely to put both the celebrators and the celebrated on a poor footing!

00:03:47.690 --> 00:03:50.690
The rice shower for luck becomes a rice soup! {zosui is unrecognizable, but it's notably different from a congee, so}

00:03:50.690 --> 00:03:53.760
The bouquet the bride tosses seems like the kind of artificial flower that blooms when put in water!

00:03:53.760 --> 00:03:58.470
There are many couples who plan on marrying in the coming month of June,

00:03:58.820 --> 00:04:04.710
so I don't think saying “June brides aren't minding TPO” is minding TPO.

00:04:05.550 --> 00:04:07.720
Well, I guess that's true.

00:04:09.070 --> 00:04:15.200
But after all, they're June brides. Getting married in June can't be bad timing.

00:04:15.820 --> 00:04:16.750
That's the point.

00:04:17.170 --> 00:04:18.540
I'm not too familiar with it,

00:04:18.540 --> 00:04:23.610
but isn't that just something that the industry distorted because business is so slow during the rainy season?

00:04:24.090 --> 00:04:29.110
It's like the TPO Hiraga Gennai came up with for the Midsummer Day of the Ox. {note---1700s multitalent who said to eat only things starting with u on said day, in order to promote the sale of eel, which is out of season during the summer}

00:04:29.620 --> 00:04:35.810
If you eat eel on the Day of the Ox, it'll sit poorly in your stomach.

00:04:36.890 --> 00:04:41.670
After that, if you go to refresh yourself by getting soba,

00:04:42.860 --> 00:04:45.210
you'll feel like it's a bad time for soba and not want to go back!

00:04:45.640 --> 00:04:50.470
You've tried to mind TPO, but in reverse, you ended up not minding it!

00:04:51.770 --> 00:04:56.270
Even when going to the bike shop to buy a bike, you can be treated like you're not minding TPO.

00:04:56.740 --> 00:04:58.090
What do you mean?

00:05:01.130 --> 00:05:03.930
Hello, I'd like to buy a moped.

00:05:06.810 --> 00:05:07.570
A moped?

00:05:07.860 --> 00:05:10.130
We don't normally sell those here.

00:05:10.130 --> 00:05:12.410
I guess we can order one for you...

00:05:12.410 --> 00:05:13.920
No, that's fine.

00:05:14.400 --> 00:05:19.580
Even though I went to a bike shop to buy a bike, I was treated like I wasn't minding my TPO!

00:05:20.520 --> 00:05:25.320
What can cause one to completely miss TPO when they're trying to mind it is a mystery!

00:05:26.690 --> 00:05:28.320
And now, the news.

00:05:28.320 --> 00:05:35.200
The fire that began before dawn today is still burning. Firefighters are still active on the scene.

00:05:35.200 --> 00:05:37.350
This BGM on the news...

00:05:37.350 --> 00:05:39.000
It's the theme from Backdraft.

00:05:39.340 --> 00:05:41.850
They wanted to keep TPO in mind when selecting music,

00:05:41.850 --> 00:05:44.190
but instead, they chose something imprudent!

00:05:45.650 --> 00:05:47.540
I wonder if they'll get complaints.

00:05:49.040 --> 00:05:51.450
Oh my, where are you going all decked out like that?

00:05:51.450 --> 00:05:53.650
To a party at a high-class hotel.

00:05:53.950 --> 00:05:58.020
Going to a party at a hotel in formal wear is minding your TPO.

00:06:01.020 --> 00:06:02.860
Formal wear, huh.

00:06:03.330 --> 00:06:07.560
If you go in formal wear to a party where comickers are gathered, you may think you're minding TPO.

00:06:07.560 --> 00:06:10.870
But instead, the result is that you aren't!

00:06:10.870 --> 00:06:12.770
The world is full of things like that!

00:06:13.200 --> 00:06:15.670
Showing up with a present on Christmas Eve,

00:06:15.670 --> 00:06:19.040
only to be told to mind the TPO and come back on the 26th!

00:06:19.040 --> 00:06:24.050
You broadcast a show in an unstable dictatorship, thinking it'll be fine because it's just a cartoon about robots.

00:06:24.050 --> 00:06:27.850
But you end up not minding the TPO when the final episode is about a revolution!

00:06:27.850 --> 00:06:31.490
Situations where you try to mind it but it comes out the other way!

00:06:31.770 --> 00:06:33.530
This comic is the same.

00:06:33.530 --> 00:06:37.290
Even if we try to be prudent and mind TPO with our gags,

00:06:37.560 --> 00:06:40.190
that kind of incident happens after printing,

00:06:40.190 --> 00:06:43.460
and by the day it goes on sale, the gags don't mind TPO!

00:06:43.860 --> 00:06:46.230
If we try to mind future TPO...

00:06:47.900 --> 00:06:50.770
We won't be able to use anything besides this type of impossible gag!

00:06:52.090 --> 00:06:52.770
Oh my.

00:06:53.210 --> 00:06:56.680
Not minding TPO certainly makes things dramatic.

00:06:57.910 --> 00:07:01.300
For example, take a 9th-grader about to take his exams... {note}

00:07:02.450 --> 00:07:05.290
And send in a sexy tutor.

00:07:05.560 --> 00:07:07.890
All right, answer the next question.

00:07:09.920 --> 00:07:12.960
Find me the volume of this cone.

00:07:12.960 --> 00:07:14.740
I can't, teacher!

00:07:14.740 --> 00:07:17.710
I can't form an image just from looking at it on paper!

00:07:18.430 --> 00:07:21.440
If I don't see it as a physical, 3D object—!

00:07:24.710 --> 00:07:26.960
Cones!

00:07:29.010 --> 00:07:31.780
These aren't cones!

00:07:31.780 --> 00:07:32.790
Their height!

00:07:32.790 --> 00:07:35.020
Let me measure their height!

00:07:35.020 --> 00:07:36.520
Oh no!

00:07:36.520 --> 00:07:39.250
The radius is &($% cm...

00:07:39.250 --> 00:07:41.360
Oh no...

00:07:44.390 --> 00:07:46.410
Oh no!

00:07:47.260 --> 00:07:50.840
Oh no! I can't study without my eraser!

00:07:50.840 --> 00:07:52.020
Excuse me!

00:07:53.900 --> 00:07:56.140
That's not an eraser!

00:07:57.640 --> 00:08:00.140
This time from behind!

00:08:00.140 --> 00:08:06.150
Sending a sexy tutor to a middle-school kid about to take his exams certainly isn't minding TPO!

00:08:06.150 --> 00:08:08.050
But isn't it exciting? {rousing?}

00:08:08.050 --> 00:08:11.220
Certainly. It seems like it'd be a popular basis for a story.

00:08:11.220 --> 00:08:13.320
Love scenes on the battlefield!

00:08:13.320 --> 00:08:16.220
It isn't the time for that kind of thing, but it's still exciting!

00:08:16.220 --> 00:08:19.240
Rather than a murder in a disorderly city,

00:08:19.240 --> 00:08:23.000
incidents in the peaceful countryside grab people's attention!

00:08:23.240 --> 00:08:25.030
Rather than games you play in your free time,

00:08:25.030 --> 00:08:27.740
games you play right before deadline are more fun!

00:08:28.110 --> 00:08:33.210
That's right. Not minding TPO is more interesting.

00:08:34.550 --> 00:08:35.680
You were there?

00:08:35.680 --> 00:08:36.810
Always.

00:08:37.190 --> 00:08:44.550
The scene in that hit movie where the heroines met was dramatic because they didn't mind TPO.

00:08:47.800 --> 00:08:49.820
Well, it was a hit.

00:08:49.820 --> 00:08:51.260
I disagree.

00:08:51.510 --> 00:08:54.850
Teacher, if you don't mind your TPO, you'll sell.

00:08:57.600 --> 00:08:59.100
Sell?

00:08:59.340 --> 00:09:00.840
But how?

00:09:00.840 --> 00:09:05.200
I was brought up well, so I'm always minding myself.

00:09:05.200 --> 00:09:09.010
There's a fast way to not mind TPO!

00:09:14.660 --> 00:09:16.900
Don't eat bleepJoy during the Sengoku period!

00:09:17.120 --> 00:09:20.120
Don't play Witch bleeping during the Sengoku period!

00:09:20.410 --> 00:09:22.710
It's simple with just a time slip!

00:09:22.710 --> 00:09:25.160
Now you're not minding TPO!

00:09:25.570 --> 00:09:28.810
That's certainly true, but that's because it's a different era!

00:09:29.030 --> 00:09:31.220
Don't text people during the Sengoku period!

00:09:31.430 --> 00:09:33.520
Don't be a shut-in during the Sengoku period!

00:09:33.730 --> 00:09:36.290
Don't read doujinshi during the Sengoku period!

00:09:38.170 --> 00:09:41.510
But there's one person who fits right in.

00:09:41.510 --> 00:09:43.090
I shall rule this country! {:[oh lol the horns}

00:09:51.590 --> 00:09:54.060
She certainly matches the era,

00:09:54.720 --> 00:09:56.940
but the art style doesn't match at all.

00:09:56.940 --> 00:09:59.730
We must keep TPO in mind while drawing.

00:10:04.440 --> 00:10:05.900
Right, right.

00:10:15.680 --> 00:10:16.580
It's the sea!

00:10:19.050 --> 00:10:19.210
The delivery of

00:10:19.210 --> 00:10:19.380
this episode,

00:10:19.380 --> 00:10:19.550
due to Happy Monday,

00:10:19.550 --> 00:10:19.680
was a great blow

00:10:19.680 --> 00:10:19.850
to the staff
(2009/7/17)

00:10:19.850 --> 00:10:20.150
Not particularly bitter about it or anything

00:10:26.050 --> 00:10:29.190
Sea Day... A Japanese holiday.

00:10:29.190 --> 00:10:30.160
A festive day.

00:10:32.990 --> 00:10:35.010
Can people from landlocked prefectures celebrate it?

00:10:36.370 --> 00:10:37.350
Er?

00:10:37.350 --> 00:10:40.430
I asked, can people from landlocked prefectures celebrate it?

00:10:40.430 --> 00:10:44.490
“As Japan is an oceanic nation, Sea Day is a celebration for all its people.”

00:10:44.490 --> 00:10:45.670
Isn't that how it is?

00:10:45.670 --> 00:10:48.380
That seems rather... indelicate.

00:10:48.820 --> 00:10:52.150
Saitama, Tochigi, Gunma, Yamanashi, Nagano, Gifu, Nara!

00:10:52.150 --> 00:10:54.920
There are seven landlocked prefectures!

00:10:55.680 --> 00:11:00.100
It's unfair to make these landlockeders celebrate Sea Day!

00:11:00.100 --> 00:11:02.720
You've been making up a lot of words lately, teacher.

00:11:03.150 --> 00:11:07.500
It's like buying a kid a game when he doesn't have the system to play it on!

00:11:07.500 --> 00:11:10.060
Or, if the whole country really does have to celebrate,{check this in case it is one of the below}

00:11:10.060 --> 00:11:12.900
why don't we make them take it all the way? Even if it's overdoing it!

00:11:12.900 --> 00:11:14.670
Don't just go and say that!

00:11:14.940 --> 00:11:18.670
And beyond that, Sea Day makes it a “Happy Monday”!

00:11:19.090 --> 00:11:20.910
But who's happy!?

00:11:20.910 --> 00:11:23.480
Because of it, deadlines get moved up a day!

00:11:23.480 --> 00:11:25.980
Just how much do you think that makes comickers suffer!

00:11:25.980 --> 00:11:29.650
Er, I mean, just how much do you think that makes the self-employed suffer!

00:11:29.930 --> 00:11:32.830
Aren't public servants the only ones who're “happy” about it!?

00:11:32.830 --> 00:11:34.390
Teacher, you're a public servant.

00:11:34.390 --> 00:11:35.920
It's a holiday we can't celebrate!

00:11:35.920 --> 00:11:37.660
There's so many like that.

00:11:38.220 --> 00:11:39.660
Certainly, in this world,

00:11:39.660 --> 00:11:43.830
there are so many things we can't 
honestly celebrate even if we wanted to.

00:11:43.830 --> 00:11:47.600
The owner of the funeral home near my house said so...

00:11:48.080 --> 00:11:50.580
This is our 30th year in business,

00:11:50.580 --> 00:11:53.340
but from the customers' standpoint, we can't celebrate.

00:11:53.620 --> 00:11:56.590
Coincidentally, we just avoided celebrating our 3000th client.

00:11:57.380 --> 00:11:58.680
Well, ummm.

00:11:58.680 --> 00:12:00.080
He's right about that.

00:12:00.080 --> 00:12:03.780
I was going to congratulate a girl from my neighbourhood,

00:12:03.780 --> 00:12:07.300
but she doesn't know who the father is.

00:12:08.290 --> 00:12:10.820
I don't know whether to celebrate it or not...

00:12:10.820 --> 00:12:13.680
A new life should be celebrated unconditionally.

00:12:14.180 --> 00:12:17.300
My dad won a contest,

00:12:20.280 --> 00:12:22.690
but I don't know whether it's good or bad to celebrate!

00:12:24.200 --> 00:12:27.750
Harumi is finally getting her debut in a magazine, but...

00:12:27.750 --> 00:12:29.900
Isn't that something to celebrate?

00:12:29.900 --> 00:12:31.580
But it's a collaboration, so... {lit. "comes with an original work"}

00:12:34.780 --> 00:12:36.380
Why is she working on -that-!?

00:12:39.610 --> 00:12:42.140
I don't know whether I should celebrate or not.

00:12:42.340 --> 00:12:45.130
Make up your mind!

00:12:45.130 --> 00:12:46.630
But there's no reason for it! {*/no excuse for saying that}

00:12:46.630 --> 00:12:52.650
Of course it's unclear whether it's good or bad to debut on a project with so little anticipation.

00:12:52.650 --> 00:12:56.880
It'd be far better to have been asked to draw something like Deableep Note.

00:12:56.880 --> 00:12:57.830
You were there?

00:12:57.830 --> 00:12:58.920
Always.

00:12:59.040 --> 00:13:00.910
Big brother, it's her first victory!

00:13:01.210 --> 00:13:03.730
My favorite horse had her first victory!

00:13:03.730 --> 00:13:05.550
Isn't that a happy occasion?

00:13:09.660 --> 00:13:12.300
And she was so popular after 300 straight losses... {note urara again}

00:13:13.420 --> 00:13:18.220
I wanted to show you the audience's dry spell, brother. {*}

00:13:18.680 --> 00:13:20.700
It certainly was a dry spell.

00:13:20.700 --> 00:13:22.640
Yes. The modern world...

00:13:22.640 --> 00:13:25.070
Is full of things that can't be celebrated even if you wanted to!

00:13:25.350 --> 00:13:28.570
Nowadays, the inflation and rising oil prices are bringing about a new mood: Self-deprivation.

00:13:31.340 --> 00:13:32.740
Nowadays, vacation days...

00:13:32.740 --> 00:13:34.740
...are becoming privation days! {here's where the pun bs gets really really deep; all of these examples are swapping shuku celebrate with shuku deprive}

00:13:37.570 --> 00:13:38.650
Privation.

00:13:38.920 --> 00:13:44.150
Vacation is limited to the small segment of the population with spare time and money.

00:13:44.150 --> 00:13:46.800
The vast majority spend their leisure time in self-deprivation,

00:13:46.800 --> 00:13:49.660
staying near home, doing sober, subdued things—privation!

00:13:49.660 --> 00:13:52.010
Like suspension from school.

00:13:52.010 --> 00:13:55.160
It's like house arrest, so I can't say you're wrong.

00:13:55.490 --> 00:13:59.270
There's no longer celebration in Japan, only deprivation!

00:13:59.270 --> 00:14:02.370
This deprivatory mood spreads throughout the world.

00:14:03.500 --> 00:14:04.310
Behold!

00:14:04.310 --> 00:14:07.310
Even if he works, he won't be rewarded, so he deprives himself of employment!

00:14:07.310 --> 00:14:09.110
{here it gets even worse, need to pun it with "congrats", going with hail/fail for now}Fail! Employment!

00:14:09.110 --> 00:14:11.310
He can't afford to get married on his low salary!

00:14:11.310 --> 00:14:13.130
Fail! Wedding!

00:14:13.130 --> 00:14:15.580
He already doesn't have enough money to pay his tuition!

00:14:15.580 --> 00:14:17.400
Fail! On getting accepted!

00:14:17.400 --> 00:14:20.590
A TV anime was too luxurious, so it was self-deprived to an OAD.

00:14:20.590 --> 00:14:22.240
Fail! Anime adaption!

00:14:22.240 --> 00:14:24.900
Road construction in this era of tight finances!

00:14:24.900 --> 00:14:26.060
Fail! Opening!

00:14:27.160 --> 00:14:30.140
...But I guess those are always still “Hail! Opening!”

00:14:30.440 --> 00:14:32.430
Those, of all things, should learn some self-deprivation!

00:14:33.430 --> 00:14:34.990
Privation's pr...

00:14:34.990 --> 00:14:36.690
That's like the pur in purge, right?

00:14:36.890 --> 00:14:38.800
It's like the pur in purge, isn't it.

00:14:38.800 --> 00:14:40.190
Didn't see that, didn't see that.

00:14:41.040 --> 00:14:44.110
Very well, how does everyone think we should spend privation days?

00:14:44.510 --> 00:14:47.380
How shall we spend privation days?

00:14:49.380 --> 00:14:53.890
I know plenty of dull ways to spend days off.

00:14:54.800 --> 00:14:56.680
Should you be out here?

00:14:56.680 --> 00:14:57.530
Huh?

00:14:57.870 --> 00:15:01.560
It's a privation day, so you shouldn't try to enjoy yourself like on a vacation day.

00:15:01.560 --> 00:15:02.730
I understand.

00:15:04.630 --> 00:15:06.230
What are you doing?

00:15:06.520 --> 00:15:10.840
Seeing how many times I can fold a chopstick wrapper.

00:15:12.120 --> 00:15:15.430
That's a really good way to spend a day of privation.

00:15:15.430 --> 00:15:18.130
The key is folding it into four even parts.

00:15:18.130 --> 00:15:18.710
Afterwards,

00:15:18.880 --> 00:15:21.820
you can write page numbers on all the pages in Magazine.

00:15:21.980 --> 00:15:24.330
And say “ah” into a fan.

00:15:24.710 --> 00:15:27.160
Take the lead out of a pencil.

00:15:27.530 --> 00:15:29.990
After that, you can make yourself look like a corpse.

00:15:29.990 --> 00:15:30.860
With chalk.

00:15:31.230 --> 00:15:32.560
{it's like} I'm closed in.

00:15:32.560 --> 00:15:37.010
That's... Somehow, that's an incredibly proper way to spend a day of privation.

00:15:37.010 --> 00:15:39.120
All right, everyone, let's all do it.

00:15:42.270 --> 00:15:44.450
Fun, isn't it?

00:15:44.450 --> 00:15:46.770
If you're having fun, it's not a proper day of privation.

00:15:48.780 --> 00:15:51.720
The pr in privation has to be the pur in purge.

00:15:49.160 --> 00:15:53.510
Teacher... have we properly spent a day of privation?

00:15:53.770 --> 00:15:58.510
Coming to the sea on Sea Day is inexcusable to people from those landlocked prefectures. {*}

00:15:58.510 --> 00:16:00.890
Can we really call it a day of privation?

00:16:00.890 --> 00:16:02.260
You almost get it.

00:16:02.520 --> 00:16:03.960
We've deprived ourselves enough.

00:16:03.960 --> 00:16:06.630
Is this not a day of privation?

00:16:13.410 --> 00:16:16.170
Have we not deprived ourselves enough?

00:16:21.100 --> 00:16:24.610
As I thought, it's impossible to 
celebrate Sea Day in the mountains.

00:16:24.970 --> 00:16:28.430
Aren't you using a broad definition of
school if you don't mind coming here?

00:16:28.430 --> 00:16:30.620
I -am- a school shut-in.

00:16:30.620 --> 00:16:33.860
The pr in privation is the same as the pur in purge.

00:16:47.290 --> 00:16:49.900
They really do connect.

00:16:50.470 --> 00:16:50.640
No self-confidence

00:16:50.640 --> 00:16:50.810
Not really feeling loved, even with a lover

00:16:50.810 --> 00:16:50.970
Thinks of their own thoughts as meaningless

00:16:50.970 --> 00:16:51.110
Cannot express their opinion

00:16:51.110 --> 00:16:51.270
Normally watches people's expressions

00:16:51.270 --> 00:16:51.570
Do not act unless ordered

00:16:55.860 --> 00:16:57.280
An overprotective group?

00:16:57.520 --> 00:17:01.920
Well... Protectors tend to be overprotective, don't they.

00:17:03.380 --> 00:17:05.490
You don't look like a protector.

00:17:05.490 --> 00:17:09.390
No, Kotonon is very overprotective of her skin.

00:17:11.770 --> 00:17:13.560
You certainly are.

00:17:13.560 --> 00:17:16.130
You're someone who's amazingly overprotective against sunburn.

00:17:16.130 --> 00:17:17.670
You might as well not come to the beach.

00:17:17.950 --> 00:17:21.500
So you mean this is a collection of such overbearing protectors?

00:17:21.500 --> 00:17:22.970
Well, it is an overprotective group.

00:17:23.840 --> 00:17:26.660
What are you overprotective of?

00:17:26.660 --> 00:17:27.620
Comics.

00:17:28.250 --> 00:17:30.030
This is my copy to save.

00:17:30.030 --> 00:17:32.910
Other than this, I have one to read and one to lend out.

00:17:33.950 --> 00:17:39.780
After this, if LEs or ones with pack-ins come out, I'll buy three of each of those too.

00:17:39.780 --> 00:17:42.020
That's certainly overprotective, isn't it.

00:17:42.020 --> 00:17:43.960
Aren't the contents the same?

00:17:44.250 --> 00:17:48.330
There's no reason to go along with unsavory sales practices.

00:17:48.330 --> 00:17:53.370
Brother, if you say that now, you won't be able to perform unsavory sales practices.

00:17:54.340 --> 00:17:58.640
If I were, perhaps, to ever write a book,

00:17:58.640 --> 00:18:03.010
I would be happier if the reader treasured their one copy forever.

00:18:03.010 --> 00:18:05.880
Still thinking you're the only one favored by God...

00:18:07.010 --> 00:18:10.220
By the way, brother, this belongs to Fujiyoshi, one of your students.

00:18:10.970 --> 00:18:13.130
She cut it out of a magazine and laminated it.

00:18:13.600 --> 00:18:15.520
That's overprotective too, isn't it.

00:18:15.520 --> 00:18:20.330
About what you just said, with the “that too”.

00:18:20.720 --> 00:18:23.910
There's a song registered with the exact same lyrics.

00:18:23.910 --> 00:18:26.330
Pay up for the reproduction rights to the music.

00:18:27.170 --> 00:18:28.140
Hey, you.

00:18:28.520 --> 00:18:30.440
About the design of your hakama.

00:18:30.750 --> 00:18:35.110
There's no way we -couldn't- consider it an infringement on one of our company's character designs.

00:18:35.410 --> 00:18:36.350
Pay up.

00:18:36.350 --> 00:18:37.440
Pay up.

00:18:37.440 --> 00:18:39.680
Aren't you being overprotective of your copyrights!?

00:18:39.970 --> 00:18:42.520
There are plenty more overprotective people here.

00:18:42.760 --> 00:18:45.560
Overprotective people who wear white gloves while playing with their toys!

00:18:45.560 --> 00:18:47.940
Those who are overprotective of problematic cabinet ministers!

00:18:47.940 --> 00:18:50.440
Those who watch cosmetics drop by drop! {note: pr campaign promoting the amount of care that went into production of Domohorn Wrinkle}

00:18:51.410 --> 00:18:53.360
I don't fit in with these people!

00:18:53.360 --> 00:18:55.220
I'm gonna go take a swim!

00:18:55.870 --> 00:18:57.870
How completely out of context.

00:18:59.130 --> 00:19:01.890
Very well. Then I'll go over there.

00:19:04.530 --> 00:19:05.540
Isn't this overprotective!?

00:19:05.990 --> 00:19:08.040
Just where am I supposed to swim!?

00:19:08.270 --> 00:19:09.110
Over here!

00:19:09.110 --> 00:19:09.780
That's narrow!

00:19:10.150 --> 00:19:11.080
What're those!?

00:19:11.380 --> 00:19:13.830
They've been increasing thanks to overprotection.

00:19:13.830 --> 00:19:15.450
The sea is no fun anymore!

00:19:15.450 --> 00:19:16.820
I'm going to the park!

00:19:19.420 --> 00:19:20.410
Where are the rides?

00:19:20.410 --> 00:19:22.540
They're dangerous, so we've removed all of them.

00:19:22.760 --> 00:19:22.990
{Temporary} Do Not Drink

00:19:23.460 --> 00:19:24.790
-All- of them!?

00:19:24.790 --> 00:19:27.380
That's just dodging responsibility in the name of being protective!

00:19:27.860 --> 00:19:29.900
There's so, so much overprotection in the world!

00:19:29.900 --> 00:19:32.400
If you fluff things up by being too overprotective,{check}

00:19:32.400 --> 00:19:34.500
doesn't that just make everyone like them less!?{check}

00:19:34.810 --> 00:19:38.070
The crazy fans scare the newbies off!

00:19:38.070 --> 00:19:40.980
Excessively being selected for the All Stars is frowned upon!{Rakuten Golden Eagles got all 8 fan's choice slots one year}

00:19:41.250 --> 00:19:44.010
Making the locals shudder during a pilgrimage!{the lucky star shrine}

00:19:44.260 --> 00:19:47.920
Laughing too much during a Kudo Kankuro movie, making it dull for the other patrons!

00:19:47.920 --> 00:19:51.250
Since everyone is overprotective, it drives down interest!

00:19:51.250 --> 00:19:56.360
Having learned that lesson, I dissolve my contract with my body double at once!

00:19:56.360 --> 00:19:57.460
Teacher.

00:20:00.480 --> 00:20:03.070
This old lady wants to thank you.

00:20:03.070 --> 00:20:03.660
Thank me?

00:20:03.980 --> 00:20:09.350
Thank you so much for visiting grandpa's grave.

00:20:09.350 --> 00:20:10.770
Er, umm...

00:20:10.770 --> 00:20:13.730
Teacher, you must be a muscleman.

00:20:15.180 --> 00:20:17.010
The body double did it, huh.

00:20:17.270 --> 00:20:20.000
Just what did that body double do?

00:20:22.040 --> 00:20:23.380
It wasn't me!

00:20:23.380 --> 00:20:25.890
It was the idiocy of someone who resembles me!

00:20:25.890 --> 00:20:28.390
You're the best!

00:20:29.190 --> 00:20:33.560
If only we had gotten a teacher like you sooner, we—

00:20:33.560 --> 00:20:35.800
Er, hello?

00:20:37.650 --> 00:20:39.380
Just what did that body double—

00:20:46.560 --> 00:20:48.840
Are you sure you're okay with me?

00:20:48.840 --> 00:20:50.550
That body double!

00:20:51.910 --> 00:20:53.490
The fireworks are starting.

00:20:53.490 --> 00:20:57.820
What? What did he do to cause this!?

00:20:58.430 --> 00:21:00.640
I had so much fun today!

00:21:00.640 --> 00:21:01.470
Doing what?

00:22:41.720 --> 00:22:44.790
The Zetsubou-sensei Drawing Song is about to start.

00:22:44.790 --> 00:22:46.980
Let's draw stealthily and match the song, okay?

00:22:48.700 --> 00:22:55.060
A tulip leans in the wind, and lays flat.

00:22:55.060 --> 00:23:01.340
A tulip leans in the wind, and lays flat.

00:23:01.340 --> 00:23:03.070
Lightning...

00:23:03.070 --> 00:23:04.700
Flash!

00:23:04.700 --> 00:23:06.230
Lightning...

00:23:06.230 --> 00:23:07.880
Flash!

00:23:07.880 --> 00:23:11.110
The rain comes pouring down.

00:23:11.110 --> 00:23:14.380
From the gaps came the leaks.

00:23:14.380 --> 00:23:17.460
Two puddles were made.

00:23:17.460 --> 00:23:20.730
Let's go fishing, there's the fish hook!

00:23:20.730 --> 00:23:25.000
With the fish we caught, we made a fish cake.

00:23:25.250 --> 00:23:28.930
It's Zetsubou-sensei!

00:23:28.930 --> 00:23:31.540
Did everyone draw well?

00:23:31.540 --> 00:23:33.540
Bye bye!
